{title: Great Are You, Lord}
{song_number: 163}
{language: en}
{tempo: 144}
{comment: David Leonard, Leslie Jordan und Jason Ingram}

{start_of_verse}
You give [A]life. You are love. [C#m7]You bring light [Bsus4]to the darkness.
You give [A]hope. You restore [C#m7]every heart [Bsus4]that is broken.
[A]And great [C#m7]are You, [Bsus4]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
It's Your [A]breath in our lungs, [C#m7]so we pour [Bsus4]out our praise,
we pour out our praise.
It's Your [A]breath in our lungs, [C#m7]so we pour [Bsus4]out our praise
to You [A]only.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[E]All the earth will shout Your praise. Our [Esus4]hearts will cry,
these bones will sing: “Great are You, [E]Lord!”
{end_of_bridge}
